ng through three points, we can use the general equation of a circle: x\u00b2 + y\u00b2 + Dx + Ey + F = 0. Plugging in each point gives three equations.\n\nLet me plug in point M:\n\n[( (2b + c)/2 )\u00b2 + (d/2)^2 ] + D*( (2b + c)/2 ) + E*(d/2) + F = 0\n\nSimilarly, plug in E:\n\n[(c/2)^2 + (d/2)^2] + D*(c/2) + E*(d/2) + F = 0\n\nPlug in C:\n\n[c\u00b2 + d\u00b2] + D*c + E*d + F = 0\n\nSo we have three equations:\n\n1) [ ( (2b + c)^2 )/4 + d\u00b2/4 ] + D*(2b + c)/2 + E*d/2 + F = 0\n\n2) [ c\u00b2/4 + d\u00b2/4 ] + D*c/2 + E*d/2 + F = 0\n\n3) c\u00b2 + d\u00b2 + D*c + E*d + F = 0\n\nLet me subtract equation 2 from equation 1 to eliminate some terms:\n\nEquation1 - Equation2:\n\n[ ( (2b + c)^2 /4 + d\u00b2/4 ) - ( c\u00b2/4 + d\u00b2/4 ) ] + [ D*(2b + c)/2 - D*c/2 ] + [ E*d/2 - E*d/2 ] + [ F - F ] = 0\n\nSimplify:\n\n[ ( (4b\u00b2 + 4bc + c\u00b2)/4 - c\u00b2/4 ) ] + [ D*(2b)/2 ] = 0\n\nSimplify the first term:\n\n(4b\u00b2 + 4bc + c\u00b2 - c\u00b2)/4 = (4b\u00b2 + 4bc)/4 = b\u00b2 + bc\n\nSecond term: D*(2b)/2 = D*b\n\nSo equation: b\u00b2 + bc + D*b = 0 => D*b = -b\u00b2 - bc => D = -b - c (assuming b \u2260 0)\n\nSimilarly, let's subtract equation 2 from equation 3:\n\nEquation3 - Equation2:\n\n[ c\u00b2 + d\u00b2 - c\u00b2/4 - d\u00b2/4 ] + [ D*c - D*c/2 ] + [ E*d - E*d/2 ] + [ F - F ] = 0\n\nSimplify:\n\n( (3c\u00b2)/4 + (3d\u00b2)/4 ) + ( D*c/2 ) + ( E*d/2 ) = 0\n\nMultiply through by 4 to eliminate denominators:\n\n3c\u00b2 + 3d\u00b2 + 2D*c + 2E*d = 0\n\nNow, from earlier, we found D = -b - c. Let's substitute D into this equation.\n\nSo:\n\n3c\u00b2 + 3d\u00b2 + 2*(-b - c)*c + 2E*d = 0\n\nSimplify:\n\n3c\u00b2 + 3d\u00b2 - 2b c - 2c\u00b2 + 2E d = 0\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n(3c\u00b2 - 2c\u00b2) + 3d\u00b2 - 2b c + 2E d = 0\n\nSo:\n\nc\u00b2 + 3d\u00b2 - 2b c + 2E d = 0\n\nWe need to solve for E. Let's hold onto this equation for now.\n\nNow, from equation2:\n\n[ c\u00b2/4 + d\u00b2/4 ] + D*c/2 + E*d/2 + F = 0\n\nWe know D = -b - c, so plug that in:\n\n[ 