ug in the known values into Ceva's formula.\n\n[sin(20\u00b0)/sin(30\u00b0)] * [sin(10\u00b0)/sin(40\u00b0)] * [sin(\u03b1)/sin(\u03b2)] = 1\n\nSo, solving for [sin(\u03b1)/sin(\u03b2)]:\n\n[sin(\u03b1)/sin(\u03b2)] = [sin(30\u00b0) * sin(40\u00b0)] / [sin(20\u00b0) * sin(10\u00b0)]\n\nCompute the right-hand side. Let's compute each term:\n\nsin(30\u00b0) = 0.5\n\nsin(40\u00b0) \u2248 0.6428\n\nsin(20\u00b0) \u2248 0.3420\n\nsin(10\u00b0) \u2248 0.1736\n\nSo, numerator: 0.5 * 0.6428 \u2248 0.3214\n\nDenominator: 0.3420 * 0.1736 \u2248 0.0595\n\nThus, [sin(\u03b1)/sin(\u03b2)] \u2248 0.3214 / 0.0595 \u2248 5.405\n\nHmm, that's approximately 5.4. So sin(\u03b1) \u2248 5.4 sin(\u03b2)\n\nBut we also know that \u03b1 + \u03b2 = 80\u00b0, so \u03b2 = 80\u00b0 - \u03b1\n\nThus, sin(\u03b1) \u2248 5.4 sin(80\u00b0 - \u03b1)\n\nUsing sine of difference: sin(80\u00b0 - \u03b1) = sin80 cos\u03b1 - cos80 sin\u03b1\n\nTherefore,\n\nsin\u03b1 \u2248 5.4 [sin80 cos\u03b1 - cos80 sin\u03b1]\n\nLet's compute sin80 and cos80:\n\nsin80 \u2248 0.9848\n\ncos80 \u2248 0.1736\n\nThus,\n\nsin\u03b1 \u2248 5.4 [0.9848 cos\u03b1 - 0.1736 sin\u03b1]\n\nBring all terms to one side:\n\nsin\u03b1 + 5.4 * 0.1736 sin\u03b1 \u2248 5.4 * 0.9848 cos\u03b1\n\nCompute coefficients:\n\nLeft side: sin\u03b1 (1 + 5.4 * 0.1736) \u2248 sin\u03b1 (1 + 0.9374) \u2248 sin\u03b1 * 1.9374\n\nRight side: 5.4 * 0.9848 cos\u03b1 \u2248 5.318 cos\u03b1\n\nThus,\n\nsin\u03b1 / cos\u03b1 \u2248 5.318 / 1.9374 \u2248 2.746\n\nTherefore, tan\u03b1 \u2248 2.746\n\nTaking arctangent:\n\n\u03b1 \u2248 arctan(2.746) \u2248 70\u00b0\n\nSince tan60\u00b0 \u2248 1.732, tan70\u00b0 \u2248 2.747, which is very close. So \u03b1 \u2248 70\u00b0, which would make \u03b2 \u2248 10\u00b0\n\nWait, so angle CAM \u2248 70\u00b0, angle BAM \u2248 10\u00b0. Let me check that. If \u03b1 is 70\u00b0, then \u03b2 is 10\u00b0, so angle BAM is 10\u00b0, angle CAM is 70\u00b0, summing to 80\u00b0, which matches angle A.\n\nSo, using Ceva's the