os \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 )^2 /4 ] [ 2 / (1 + cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nSimplify:\n\nBD^2 = [ (1 + cos \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 )^2 * 2 ] / [4(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ] = [ (1 + cos \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 )^2 ] / [2(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nTherefore, BD = (1 + cos \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 ) / sqrt[2(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nHmm. This seems complicated. Maybe there's a trigonometric identity to simplify this.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute BC - AB.\n\nFirst, compute BC. Points B(cos \u03b8, sin \u03b8) and C(-1,0). Distance BC:\n\nsqrt[ ( -1 - cos \u03b8 )^2 + ( 0 - sin \u03b8 )^2 ] = sqrt[ (1 + 2 cos \u03b8 + cos\u00b2 \u03b8 ) + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 ] = sqrt[ 2 + 2 cos \u03b8 ] = sqrt[2(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nSimilarly, AB is the distance between A(1,0) and B(cos \u03b8, sin \u03b8):\n\nsqrt[ (cos \u03b8 -1)^2 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 ] = sqrt[ cos\u00b2 \u03b8 - 2 cos \u03b8 +1 + sin\u00b2 \u03b8 ] = sqrt[ 2 - 2 cos \u03b8 ] = sqrt[2(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nThus, BC = sqrt[2(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ] and AB = sqrt[2(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nTherefore, BC - AB = sqrt[2(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ] - sqrt[2(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ] = sqrt(2)[ sqrt(1 + cos \u03b8 ) - sqrt(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nCompute (BC - AB)/2:\n\n[ sqrt(2)/2 ][ sqrt(1 + cos \u03b8 ) - sqrt(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ] = [1/\u221a2][ sqrt(1 + cos \u03b8 ) - sqrt(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nCompare this to BD. Earlier, we found BD = (1 + cos \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 ) / sqrt[2(1 + cos \u03b8 ) ]\n\nWait, maybe we can manipulate BD to see if it's equal to (BC - AB)/2.\n\nLet me compute (BC - AB)/2:\n\nFirst, sqrt(1 + cos \u03b8 ) = sqrt(2 cos\u00b2 (\u03b8/2) ) = \u221a2 cos(\u03b8/2 )\n\nSimilarly, sqrt(1 - cos \u03b8 ) = sqrt(2 sin\u00b2 (\u03b8/2) ) = \u221a2 sin(\u03b8/2 )\n\nThus,\n\n(BC - AB)/2 = [ sqrt(2) ( sqrt(1 + cos \u03b8 ) - sqrt(1 - cos \u03b8 ) ) ] /2 = [ sqrt(2)(\u221a2 cos(\u03b8/2 ) - \u221a2 sin(\u03b8/2 )) ] /2 = [ 2( cos(\u03b8/2 ) - sin(\u03b8/2 ) ) ] /2 = cos(\u03b8/2 ) - sin(\u03b8/2 )\n\nNow, let's compute BD:\n\nWe had BD = (1 + cos \u03b8 - sin \u03b8 ) / sqrt[2(1 +